      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "This is expected with the release binaries. `bitcoin-qt` from https://bitcoincore.org/ is built against a static Qt that includes only the `xcb` (X11) and `minimal` platform plugins, as your error output shows. There is no native Wayland plugin, so forcing `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland` will always abort. Adding Wayland support to the release builds is tracked in bitcoin/bitcoin#19950.\n\nAs a workaround, try forcing the X11 backend (via XWayland):\n```console\n$ QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb ~/bitcoin/bitcoin-31.1/bin/bitcoin-qt\n```\n\nIf it still fails with the `xcb` plugin, please re-run with plugin debugging and post the output:\n```console\n$ QT_DEBUG_PLUGINS=1 QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb ~/bitcoin/bitcoin-31.1/bin/bitcoin-qt\n```\n\nA common cause of such failures is a missing XCB runtime library. For example, Qt 6's `xcb` plugin needs `libxcb-cursor0`. Installing it may fix this:\n```console\n$ sudo apt install libxcb-cursor0\n```\n\nIf you want native Wayland now, you can build `bitcoin-qt` from source.",
